{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/6lkrit8v","slideIndex":12,"position":{"left":70,"top":226,"width":1140,"height":270},"text":"SELECT u.name, COUNT(*) AS completed_donations\nFROM Users u\nJOIN FoodDonations d ON d.donor_id = u.user_id\nWHERE d.status = 'DELIVERED'\nGROUP BY u.user_id, u.name;","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":29,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#194D3B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7mdsry9g","slideIndex":12,"position":{"left":70,"top":534,"width":1120,"height":62},"text":"Result: completed donation counts for each donor with at least one delivery.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#253C33","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/snm9k3q1","slideIndex":12,"position":{"left":70,"top":613,"width":1120,"height":38},"text":"Meals rescued must use a documented estimate and consistent quantity units.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#C56B36","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i6imtj","slideIndex":12,"text":"\nSource: FoodBridge project brief supplied by the team. Technical structures and examples describe a proposed design, not verified implementation.\nThis query is valid for the proposed schema and includes donors who have completed donations. A LEFT JOIN with a condition in the JOIN can include donors with zero completed donations. Do not add kilograms and servings as if they were the same unit. A meal estimate must state a conversion factor and avoid presenting the estimate as an observed count."}
