{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/otrqk1","slideIndex":14,"text":"\nSource: FoodBridge project brief supplied by the team. Technical structures and examples describe a proposed design, not verified implementation.\nA unique email constraint creates a useful lookup index. Index foreign-key columns as needed and inspect actual query plans. More indexes consume storage and make writes more expensive. Location matching can begin with city or area filters, then add distance queries when location data is defined. Spring Security handles authentication and authorization, but the service must also check object ownership."}
